@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="container privacy-policy">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> September 2026 </p>

    <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how [Library App Name]
        ("we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, stores, and protects
        your personal information when you use our mobile application,
        website, and related services (collectively, the "Service").
    </p>

    <p>
        By using the Service, you agree to the practices described in
        this Privacy Policy.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

    <p>We may collect the following information:</p>

    <h3>Information You Provide</h3>

    <ul>
        <li>Name or username</li>
        <li>Email address</li>
        <li>Password or authentication details</li>
        <li>Library membership or account number</li>
        <li>Profile information</li>
        <li>
            Books added to your library, reading lists, favorites,
            or borrowing history
        </li>
        <li>Messages, feedback, or support requests</li>
        <li>Any other information you voluntarily submit</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Information Collected Automatically</h3>

    <p>
        When you use the Service, we may automatically collect:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Device type and operating system</li>
        <li>App version</li>
        <li>IP address</li>
        <li>Browser type</li>
        <li>Language and time zone</li>
        <li>Usage information and interactions with the Service</li>
        <li>Crash reports and diagnostic information</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Information from Third Parties</h3>

    <p>
        If you sign in through a third-party service, such as Google,
        Apple, or Facebook, we may receive information that you
        authorize that service to share with us, such as your name,
        email address, and profile image.
    </p>

    <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>

    <p>We may use your information to:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Create and manage your account</li>
        <li>Provide, maintain, and improve the Service</li>
        <li>
            Help you search for, reserve, borrow, or manage library
            materials
        </li>
        <li>Track reading lists, favorites, and account activity</li>
        <li>Send service-related notifications and updates</li>
        <li>Respond to questions and support requests</li>
        <li>Personalize your experience</li>
        <li>
            Detect, prevent, and address fraud, misuse, security
            incidents, or technical problems
        </li>
        <li>
            Analyze usage trends and improve the performance of the
            Service
        </li>
        <li>Comply with applicable legal obligations</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        We will not use your personal information for purposes
        unrelated to the Service without providing appropriate notice
        or obtaining consent where required by law.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Legal Basis for Processing</h2>

    <p>
        Where applicable, we process personal information based on one
        or more of the following:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Your consent</li>
        <li>The performance of a contract with you</li>
        <li>Our legitimate business interests</li>
        <li>Compliance with legal obligations</li>
        <li>
            Protection of your vital interests or the rights and safety
            of others
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        You may withdraw consent at any time where processing is based
        on consent.
    </p>

    <h2>4. How We Share Your Information</h2>

    <p>We may share your information with:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>
            Service providers that help us operate, maintain, analyze,
            or secure the Service
        </li>
        <li>
            Libraries, institutions, or organizations connected to your
            account or library membership
        </li>
        <li>
            Authentication, hosting, analytics, notification, and
            customer-support providers
        </li>
        <li>
            Government authorities, courts, or law-enforcement agencies
            when required by law
        </li>
        <li>
            Professional advisers, such as lawyers, auditors, or
            insurers
        </li>
        <li>
            A successor organization in connection with a merger,
            acquisition, restructuring, or sale of assets
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        We do not sell your personal information. We do not share your
        library activity or reading history with third parties for
        advertising purposes unless you have given permission or
        disclosure is legally required.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Library Records and Reading Activity</h2>

    <p>
        We treat borrowing records, reading history, saved books, and
        other library activity as confidential, except when disclosure
        is:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Authorized by you</li>
        <li>Necessary to provide the requested Service</li>
        <li>Required by law, court order, or legal process</li>
        <li>
            Necessary to protect the rights, safety, or security of the
            Service or another person
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        You may be able to delete or manage certain records through
        your account settings. Some records may need to be retained
        for legal, security, accounting, or operational purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>

    <p>
        We may use cookies, software development kits, local storage,
        and similar technologies to:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Keep you signed in</li>
        <li>Remember your preferences</li>
        <li>
            Understand how users interact with the Service
        </li>
        <li>Improve functionality and performance</li>
        <li>Detect security issues</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        You may be able to control cookies through your browser or
        device settings. Disabling certain technologies may affect the
        functionality of the Service.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>

    <p>
        We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably
        necessary to:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Provide the Service</li>
        <li>Maintain your account</li>
        <li>
            Fulfill the purposes described in this Privacy Policy
        </li>
        <li>
            Comply with legal, accounting, or reporting requirements
        </li>
        <li>Resolve disputes</li>
        <li>Enforce our agreements</li>
        <li>
            Protect against fraud and security threats
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        When information is no longer required, we may delete it,
        anonymize it, or securely store it until deletion is possible.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Data Security</h2>

    <p>
        We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational
        safeguards to protect personal information from unauthorized
        access, loss, misuse, alteration, or disclosure.
    </p>

    <p>
        However, no method of transmission or electronic storage is
        completely secure. We cannot guarantee absolute security of
        your information.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Your Rights and Choices</h2>

    <p>
        Depending on your location, you may have the right to:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Access the personal information we hold about you</li>
        <li>Correct inaccurate or incomplete information</li>
        <li>Request deletion of your personal information</li>
        <li>Request restriction of certain processing</li>
        <li>Object to certain uses of your information</li>
        <li>Receive a portable copy of your information</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent</li>
        <li>Opt out of marketing communications</li>
        <li>
            Lodge a complaint with a data protection authority
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        To exercise your rights, contact us using the details below.
        We may need to verify your identity before completing your
        request.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Account Deletion</h2>

    <p>
        You may request deletion of your account by contacting us at
        [Privacy Email Address] or by using the account-deletion option
        in the Service, if available.
    </p>

    <p>
        Deleting your account may remove access to your profile, saved
        items, preferences, and other account information. We may retain
        certain information where required by law or reasonably
        necessary for legitimate business purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Children's Privacy</h2>

    <p>
        The Service is not intended for children under the age of
        [insert applicable age], unless expressly stated otherwise.
    </p>

    <p>
        We do not knowingly collect personal information from children
        without appropriate parental or guardian consent where required
        by law. If you believe that a child has provided us with
        personal information, please contact us so that we can take
        appropriate action.
    </p>

    <h2>12. International Data Transfers</h2>

    <p>
        Your information may be processed or stored in countries other
        than the country in which you live. Where required by law, we
        use appropriate safeguards for international transfers of
        personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Third-Party Links and Services</h2>

    <p>
        The Service may contain links to third-party websites,
        applications, or services. We are not responsible for the
        privacy practices, content, or security of third parties.
    </p>

    <p>
        We encourage you to review the privacy policies of any
        third-party service before providing personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

    <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we
        make changes, we will update the Effective Date and, where
        appropriate, notify you through the Service or by other
        reasonable means.
    </p>

    <p>
        Your continued use of the Service after the updated Privacy
        Policy becomes effective means that you acknowledge the
        changes.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Contact Us</h2>

    <p>
        If you have questions, concerns, or requests regarding this
        Privacy Policy or your personal information, contact us at:
    </p>

    <p>
        <strong>Admin</strong><br />
        Organization: Library<br />
        Email: manager@library.com<br />
        Address: Ellengowan Drive, Brinkin NT 0810<br />
        Website: library_App.com
    </p>
</div>
